            <ArticleTitle>Case report of trigeminal neuralgia presenting as odontalgia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>245-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of trigeminal neuralgia presenting as odontalgia in a 47-year-old female is described. This case shows the difficulty of making a correct diagnosis and how patients can be subjected to unnecessary treatment and continued suffering when a correct diagnosis is not made.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
